  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 437 AM EDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nA typical sea-breeze-driven convective pattern is expected to \npersist through next week. Under prevailing easterly flow, early \nmorning showers remain possible over the Atlantic waters and coastal \nareas each day, giving way to scattered afternoon showers and \nthunderstorms across the interior and Southwest Florida.\n\nGuidance continues to indicate a plume of Saharan dust will be \napproaching South Florida toward the middle of the work week. This \ninflux of drier could potentially suppress overall convective \ncoverage through Friday. Heat will remain the primary forecast \nconcern through next week, with maximum temperatures hovering in the \nmid-90s and peak heat indices ranging between 100-105 F for much of \nthe region, except along the immediate Atlantic coast.",
